{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I appeared.</b> In the vision that precedes prophecy, as in וַיֵּרָא אֵלָיו ה׳ (Genesis 18:1)." "<b>As El Shaddai.</b> Which indicates that I brought all of existence into being, as explained in the portion of לֶךְ לְךָ (Genesis 17:1)." "<b>But My name YHWH I did not make known to them.</b> The bet of בְּאֵל שַׁדַּי attaches to the word וּשְׁמִי. He says: and by My name YHWH I did not make Myself known to them in that vision, nor did I alter on their behalf any of the natures of imperishable things. Therefore it is fitting that I make this known to their offspring, who did not receive this from their fathers, in order to establish them for Me as a people, and so I shall redeem them."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:33.738266200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}